ent.<br>4. villages: Market towns such as Norcia, with 2146 residents in 1736 Ancona, which held 20,000 people in the mid-seventeenth century, had declined to about 7,000 inhabitants around 1700, following papal suppression of religious and ethnic minorities there.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2379, 'temperature': 0.2})
