Kwararafa is the Hausa name for the Jukun people and their capital, as well as for their kingdom. When the city was abandoned at the end of the eighteenth century, its still-extant successor town, Wukari, grew up in the same region.”  “He further notes that the next statement of the Chronicle with regard to Kwararafa was in the reign of Dauda (1421-38). It was purported that under Queen Amina of Zaria, all the towns, as far as Kwararafa and Nupe were conquered.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2644, 'temperature': 0.2})
